### Start next

**Phase 12 — Beautiful Typography & RoboText**, continuing at **12.21 Text-selection mapping** (12.1 raster quality through 12.20 vertical writing are landed: pack, face binding, RoboText architecture, Unicode/font integration, script and direction runs, bidi, the feature model, GSUB, GPOS, ligatures, kerning, the finalized run with the list over it, the measurement engine over that list, the display list that carries shaped glyph runs, the CSS font request with the face it resolves to, the deterministic conformance corpus that proves every layer from Unicode to the pen, Arabic and Devanagari shaped by a *plan* — stages of positionally masked features with the reorders between them — and a writing-mode-neutral text model where a vertical run is the same `GlyphRun` on the other axis and a sideways glyph's quarter turn is carried to the rasterizer and applied to its outline).

| | |
|---|---|
| **Why first** | Bad fonts block every “beautiful OS” claim; input and JS on ugly text waste effort |
| **Modules** | `Runtime/Source/RoboGraphics/` (glyph AA) → `RoboFont/` (face pack) → `RoboText/` (shaping) → paint/layout bridge → desktop chrome |
| **Build / test** | `BuildFont.ps1` / `TestFont.ps1`, then text/graphics/paint suites as each goal lands; visual screenshots of desktop labels |
| **Contract** | Retire cmap-per-codepoint as the **default** paint path once glyph runs exist; keep Phase 5 API; consume Unicode from Phase 4 |
| **Done when** | Shell + document Latin text looks sharp at UI sizes; Inter/SF-class pack ships under `/System/Fonts/`; shaped runs feed paint |
| **Then** | Phase 13 RoboInput → Phase 14 Beautiful Desktop Shell → Phase 15 Compositor (smooth beauty) → Phase 16 RoboJS → … |

Phase **0–11** remain complete. Kernel Category A drivers stay outside this beauty track.

